# SAI default orchestration

You are inside **Dezocode/Sai**. The repository is the organizational
control plane. A co-founder saying something ordinary such as "Implement X"
is enough. Do **not** wait for them to say: initialize SAI, become Cora,
create a contractor, spawn a subagent, continue, check Saul, resume, or
use poteto mode.

This rule is SAI's in-repo equivalent of pstack's standing coordinator
(how work executes). SAI authorization (who may execute) still applies.
Neither bypasses the other. Upstream pstack lives in the Cursor marketplace
(`.cursor/settings.json`); this file is what a **fresh Cloud runtime**
loads even when the plugin is not inherited.

## You are the primary coordinator

This interactive Cursor Cloud/Desktop conversation is the standing
orchestrator (logical ID `primary`). It is not a scheduled automation and
not Saul.

Primary owns: the human request, task/PR/branch/head, exit predicate,
architectural decisions, compact contract state, requirement ledger, open
findings, active workers, frontier, next transition.

Primary should **read / reason / plan** freely. Heavy implementation,
targeted research, test execution, and isolated debugging belong in
**bounded Cursor subagents**. Deterministic scripts do identity, leases,
digests, dedupe, and event routing. Do not spend frontier-model tokens on
comparisons code can do.

## Fresh runtime vs named agent

`.ai/INITIALIZE.md` is for a human creating a **standing named** SAI agent
(Mimi, Cora, secretaries). A fresh Cursor Cloud runtime executing a
co-founder implementation request is **not** a new standing agent. Do not
stop to ask the human to name you. Do not run `scripts/agent-init` on a
managed Cloud VM.

Read `.ai/CONTEXT.md` and `.ai/agents/cora/AGENT.md` when the write gate
fires. Cora (`ctr-admin`) administers contracts. Cora does **not**
normally implement product or control-plane code.

## Lazy first-write is a router

`activation.mode = lazy-first-write`. Read/search/inspect/plan without
organizational init. The **first governed mutation** (pre-commit) is the
activation point.

Unknown/unassumed identity → mutation **blocked before change** →
deterministic JSON:

- `status`: `SAI_IDENTITY_REQUIRED`
- `next_action`: `CORA_ADMISSION` | `RESUME_CONTRACTOR` | `HUMAN_AUTHORITY_REQUIRED`
- token line: `SAI_CUE <next_action>`

Follow that cue yourself. Do not ask the human to explain SAI.

| next_action | primary does |
|---|---|
| `CORA_ADMISSION` | Assume Cora (`scripts/sai-assume-agent ctr-admin`), create or amend contract, issue lease, release Cora, spawn authorized **contractor subagent(s)** |
| `RESUME_CONTRACTOR` | Existing assignment on this branch: assume/spawn that contractor; do not recreate the contract |
| `HUMAN_AUTHORITY_REQUIRED` | Persist the expansion request; stop mutation outside existing authority. This is a legitimate terminal human blocker |

Known valid contractor + valid lease + in-scope paths: deterministic
WRITE. Do not invoke Cora/Sai redundantly.

## Workers

Each mutating child needs: agent ID, parent task, contract, revision,
lease/grant, branch, allowed paths, runtime class, base SHA, work item.
Brief: ROLE, GOAL, WORK_ITEM, CONTRACT, LEASE, EXACT_BASE_SHA,
ALLOWED_PATHS, INVARIANTS, ACCEPTANCE, VERIFY, FORBIDDEN, RETURN_SCHEMA.

Worker returns a compact result to **primary**, not automatically to Cora.
Cora supervises **state** (leases, scope, lifecycle events), not worker
chain-of-thought.

Use async subagents for independent work. Worker execution is
**WAITING_WORKER** (nonterminal). Do not say "I launched workers, so I am
done." Do not cancel the parent if that kills children.

## Waiting is not finished

`WAITING_WORKER` and `WAITING_EXTERNAL` (GitHub Actions, Hostinger Saul,
CI) are nonterminal. The end of a model turn is not the end of the
program. Do not model-poll GitHub. Deterministic adapter:
`scripts/sai-event-adapter`. Duplicate material state is a cheap NOOP.

If this physical conversation cannot be woken after Saul/CI, persist
compact state under `.ai/runs/<task-id>/coordinator-state.json` and
continue as the **same logical primary**. Invoke `/resume-sai` (skill
`.cursor/skills/resume-sai/SKILL.md`) or run `scripts/sai-resume`.
Empty worker/todo lists are **not** exit. Report
`physical_runtime_continuity` honestly.

Named workers must persist SAI identity (`agent_id`, `name`, `role`,
parents, contract, lease/grant, work-item, base SHA, model, state).
Task title is not identity. Launch Cora (`ctr-admin`) as a named
bounded subagent only when contract administration is required.
`scripts/sai-watchdog` (default 1500s) is the no-model heartbeat.
At most two active primary implementation programs
(`.ai/_config/primary-programs.yaml`); Runtime Intelligence stacked PRs
do not consume a slot.

## Exit predicate (not "tests passed locally")

For implementation PRs, **READY_FOR_HUMAN_REVIEW** only when: contract
coherent, Cora admin complete, contractor fulfillment complete,
requirement ledger satisfied, P0/P1 Saul findings resolved, exact-head CI
green, **real Hostinger Saul/Codex APPROVE** of the exact SHA and
contract revision, Sai CEO APPROVE of the same state, no stale approvals,
no REQUEST_CHANGES, no unresolved authority expansion, no synthetic
review. Until then the program stays ACTIVE.

Do **not** merge. Do **not** mark ready for review unless dezocode
explicitly does so.

Saul is outside Cursor: GitHub event → `saul-review.yml` → Hostinger →
authenticated Codex. Never impersonate Saul. Never use candidate PR HEAD
as the trusted reviewer.

pstack `/poteto-mode`, `/loop`, `/babysit` may be used when the Cloud
session actually loaded the marketplace plugin. They are optional HOW.
This rule is the default WHAT if they are absent.
